{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChLs2atC81KYmWRKs14je","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"`Line.is_parallel` now raises `TypeError('Must pass only LinearEntity objects')` when either argument isn't a `LinearEntity`. I didn't run the issue's example directly. The existing `tests/test_line.py` passes (36 tests).\n\nThe same check guards all four methods in `sympy/geometry/line.py`: `is_parallel`, `is_perpendicular`, `angle_between` and `smallest_angle_between`. In each, the condition used `and`, so it only raised when both arguments were invalid. A valid first argument with a `Point` second argument got past it and hit the `AttributeError`. I changed `and` to `or` in all four places.\n\nI didn't add a test for the invalid-input case."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":316,"cache_read_input_tokens":19842,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":316},"output_tokens":236,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f9b86d10-823c-4a13-9be1-a3693fa18bc2","uuid":"8f3ed9c8-a3bc-4a19-9926-cec9ccf6cf51","timestamp":"2026-11-24T01:11:43.175Z","request_id":"req_011ChLs2akVfoCTqYPHgT5L9"}
